IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc3-interpretation`

-- ccc3-financing.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II.1 Terrorism, "Financing of Terrorism": sections 83.02, 83.03 and 83.04 (the offences).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), written by part agent ccc3 from the text alone. Imports the core and this part's own `ccc3-interpretation`.
-- The text is a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
--
-- READING A RESULT. Each offence function answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE (every element is made out), JUST FALSE (this section does not
-- make the person guilty on these facts; NEVER "not guilty of anything"), NOTHING (the answer turns on a term another section defines and the
-- caller could not say). An unmet element is read as the text's "no" because the section defines the offence by "Every person ... who ..."
-- (fork F-ccc3-1, and the marginal readings in NOTES.md). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Each section also gives `the class of the offence` and `the punishment of the offence` (core types), which parts ccc14, ccc20, ccc21,
-- ccc26 and ccc1 ask of the offence sections (PLAN.md section 6, "other parts ask this part").
-- Judgments the text hands to a court ("wilfully", "without lawful justification or excuse") are plain facts the person states.

§ `Section 83.02 -- Providing or collecting property for certain activities`

-- "directly or indirectly" and "in whole or in part" widen the manner and the extent and restrict nothing: they are not elements.

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.02(a) the use would carry out an offence referred to in subparagraphs (a)(i) to (ix) | s 83.02(a)
-- src:1294 | (a) an act or omission that constitutes an offence referred to in subparagraphs (a)(i) to (ix) of the definition of terrorist activity in subsection 83.01(1), or
@ref s 83.02(a) (src:1294)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 83.01(1)(a) listed offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.02(a) the use would carry out an offence referred to in subparagraphs (a)(i) to (ix)` MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `s 83.01(1)(a)(x) financing of terrorism (subsection 7(3.73); United Nations, 1999)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subparagraphs (a)(i) to (ix) of the definition of terrorist activity"
    WHEN `s 83.01(1)(a) none of the offences listed in subparagraphs (i) to (x)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subparagraphs (a)(i) to (ix) of the definition of terrorist activity"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.02(b) the use would carry out another act intended to cause death or serious bodily harm | s 83.02(b)
-- src:1295 | (b) any other act or omission intended to cause death or serious bodily harm to a civilian or to any other person not taking an active part in the hostilities in a situation of armed conflict, if the purpose of that act or omission, by its nature or context, is to intimidate the public, or to compel a government or an international organization to do or refrain from doing any act.
@ref s 83.02(b) (src:1295)
DECLARE `s 83.02(b) facts` HAS
    `the act or omission is intended to cause death or serious bodily harm to a civilian or to any other person not taking an active part in the hostilities in a situation of armed conflict`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the purpose of that act or omission, by its nature or context, is to intimidate the public, or to compel a government or an international organization to do or refrain from doing any act`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 83.02(b) (src:1295)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 83.02(b) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.02(b) the use would carry out another act or omission intended to cause death or serious bodily harm` MEANS
    IF     facts's `the act or omission is intended to cause death or serious bodily harm to a civilian or to any other person not taking an active part in the hostilities in a situation of armed conflict`
       AND facts's `the purpose of that act or omission, by its nature or context, is to intimidate the public, or to compel a government or an international organization to do or refrain from doing any act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the purpose of that act or omission, by its nature or context, is to intimidate the public, or to compel a government or an international organization to do or refrain from doing any act"

-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-1 | s 83.02 the person is guilty of the offence | s 83.02
-- src:1292 | Providing or collecting property for certain activities
-- src:1293 | 83.02 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years who, directly or indirectly, wilfully and without lawful justification or excuse, provides or collects property intending that it be used or knowing that it will be used, in whole or in part, in order to carry out
@ref s 83.02 (src:1292-1293)
DECLARE `s 83.02 facts` HAS
    `provides or collects property`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `does so wilfully`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `has lawful justification or excuse`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `intends that the property be used`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows that the property will be used`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence the use would carry out, if any`                             IS A `s 83.01(1)(a) listed offence`
    `the other act or omission the use would carry out`                       IS A `s 83.02(b) facts`

@ref s 83.02 (src:1292-1293)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 83.02 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.02 the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF     facts's `provides or collects property`
       AND facts's `does so wilfully`
       AND NOT facts's `has lawful justification or excuse`
       AND (facts's `intends that the property be used` OR facts's `knows that the property will be used`)
       AND (    `s 83.02(a) the use would carry out an offence referred to in subparagraphs (a)(i) to (ix)` (facts's `the offence the use would carry out, if any`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
             OR `s 83.02(b) the use would carry out another act or omission intended to cause death or serious bodily harm` (facts's `the other act or omission the use would carry out`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years who"

-- The class and the punishment (the section states no minimum imprisonment, no fine, and no minimum fine).
@ref s 83.02 (src:1293)
`s 83.02 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 83.02 (src:1293)
`s 83.02 the punishment of the offence` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 83.03 -- Providing, making available, etc., property or services for terrorist purposes`

-- The acts of (1) and (2) are the same five: "collects property or provides, invites a person to provide or makes available property or financial or other related services".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-1 | s 83.03(1) the person is guilty of the offence | s 83.03(1)
-- src:1296 | Providing, making available, etc., property or services for terrorist purposes
-- src:1297 | 83.03 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years who, directly or indirectly, wilfully and without lawful justification or excuse, collects property or provides, invites a person to provide or makes available property or financial or other related services, intending that they be used, or knowing that they will be used, in whole or in part, for the purpose of facilitating or carrying out any terrorist activity, or for the purpose of benefiting any person who is facilitating or carrying out such an activity.
@ref s 83.03(1) (src:1296-1297)
DECLARE `s 83.03 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.03 collects property`
    `s 83.03 provides property or financial or other related services`
    `s 83.03 invites a person to provide property or financial or other related services`
    `s 83.03 makes available property or financial or other related services`
    `s 83.03 does none of those things`

@ref s 83.03(1) (src:1296-1297)
DECLARE `s 83.03(1) facts` HAS
    `what the person does`                                                    IS A `s 83.03 act`
    `does so wilfully`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `has lawful justification or excuse`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `intends that they be used`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows that they will be used`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the purpose is facilitating or carrying out any terrorist activity`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the purpose is benefiting any person who is facilitating or carrying out such an activity`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 83.03(1) (src:1296-1297)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 83.03(1) facts`
      `the person is within subsection (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.03(1) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is within subsection (4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to a person who carries out any of the acts referred to in those subsections for the sole purpose of carrying out humanitarian assistance activities"
    ELSE IF     NOT (facts's `what the person does` EQUALS `s 83.03 does none of those things`)
            AND facts's `does so wilfully`
            AND NOT facts's `has lawful justification or excuse`
            AND (facts's `intends that they be used` OR facts's `knows that they will be used`)
            AND (facts's `the purpose is facilitating or carrying out any terrorist activity` OR facts's `the purpose is benefiting any person who is facilitating or carrying out such an activity`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years who"

@ref s 83.03(1) (src:1297)
`s 83.03(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 83.03(1) (src:1297)
`s 83.03(1) the punishment of the offence` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- Subsection (4) disapplies (1) and (2); it is a gate on its own facts: the "sole purpose" and "while using reasonable efforts" are both required.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.03(4) subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to a person carrying out humanitarian assistance activities | s 83.03(4)
-- src:1302 | Exception — humanitarian assistance activities
-- src:1303 | (4) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to a person who carries out any of the acts referred to in those subsections for the sole purpose of carrying out humanitarian assistance activities conducted under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law while using reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups.
@ref s 83.03(4) (src:1302-1303)
DECLARE `s 83.03(4) facts` HAS
    `carries out the acts for the sole purpose of carrying out humanitarian assistance activities conducted under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `uses reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups`                                    IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 83.03(4) (src:1302-1303)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 83.03(4) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.03(4) subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to a person carrying out humanitarian assistance activities` MEANS
    IF     facts's `carries out the acts for the sole purpose of carrying out humanitarian assistance activities conducted under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law`
       AND facts's `uses reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "do not apply to a person who carries out any of the acts referred to in those subsections for the sole purpose of carrying out humanitarian assistance activities"

-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.03(3) subsection (2) does not apply to a person acting under and in accordance with an authorization | s 83.03(3)
-- src:1300 | Exception — authorization
-- src:1301 | (3) Subsection (2) does not apply to a person who carries out any of the acts referred to in that subsection under and in accordance with an authorization granted under section 83.032.
@ref s 83.03(3) (src:1300-1301)
GIVEN `carries out the acts under and in accordance with an authorization granted under section 83.032` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.03(3) subsection (2) does not apply to a person acting under and in accordance with an authorization` MEANS
    IF `carries out the acts under and in accordance with an authorization granted under section 83.032`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to a person who carries out any of the acts referred to in that subsection under and in accordance with an authorization"

-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-1 | s 83.03(2) the person is guilty of the offence | s 83.03(2)
-- src:1298 | Providing, making available, etc., property or services — use by terrorist group
-- src:1299 | (2) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years who, directly or indirectly, wilfully and without lawful justification or excuse, collects property or provides, invites a person to provide or makes available property or financial or other related services, knowing that, in whole or part, they will be used by or will benefit a terrorist group.
@ref s 83.03(2) (src:1298-1299)
DECLARE `s 83.03(2) facts` HAS
    `what the person does`                                                    IS A `s 83.03 act`
    `does so wilfully`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `has lawful justification or excuse`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows that, in whole or part, they will be used by or will benefit the group`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 83.03(2) (src:1298-1299)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 83.03(2) facts`
      `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is within subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is within subsection (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.03(2) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF (`the person is within subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within subsection (4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) does not apply to a person who carries out any of the acts referred to in that subsection under and in accordance with an authorization"
    ELSE IF     NOT (facts's `what the person does` EQUALS `s 83.03 does none of those things`)
            AND facts's `does so wilfully`
            AND NOT facts's `has lawful justification or excuse`
            AND facts's `knows that, in whole or part, they will be used by or will benefit the group`
         THEN CONSIDER `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "knowing that, in whole or part, they will be used by or will benefit a terrorist group"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group is a terrorist group is for s 83.01(1) and is not determined
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years who"

@ref s 83.03(2) (src:1299)
`s 83.03(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 83.03(2) (src:1299)
`s 83.03(2) the punishment of the offence` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 83.04 -- Using or possessing property for terrorist purposes`

-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-1 | s 83.04 the person is guilty of the offence | s 83.04*
-- src:1442 | Using or possessing property for terrorist purposes
-- src:1443 | 83.04 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years who
-- src:1444 | (a) uses property, directly or indirectly, in whole or in part, for the purpose of facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity, or
-- src:1445 | (b) possesses property intending that it be used or knowing that it will be used, directly or indirectly, in whole or in part, for the purpose of facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity.
@ref s 83.04 (src:1442-1445)
DECLARE `s 83.04 facts` HAS
    `uses property, directly or indirectly, in whole or in part, for the purpose of facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `possesses property`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `intends that it be used for that purpose`                                IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `knows that it will be used for that purpose`                             IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)

@ref s 83.04 (src:1442-1445)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 83.04 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.04 the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF     facts's `uses property, directly or indirectly, in whole or in part, for the purpose of facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity`
       OR (facts's `possesses property` AND (facts's `intends that it be used for that purpose` OR facts's `knows that it will be used for that purpose`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years who"

@ref s 83.04 (src:1443)
`s 83.04 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 83.04 (src:1443)
`s 83.04 the punishment of the offence` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
